# Paytm Ek Photo Dukaan - environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or paste into Vercel -> Settings ->
# Environment Variables for a deployment. Every variable here is optional:
# the app boots and demos correctly with none of them set. Nothing below is
# a secret in this repo; do not commit a filled-in .env file.
#
# Only variables actually read by the code are listed. Verify with:
#   rg -n "import\.meta\.env|process\.env" src api server

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client (bundled into the browser build - never put a secret in a VITE_ var)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Payee UPI ID encoded into every `upi://pay` QR the app renders.
# Read by: src/services/paytm/upi.ts
# Fallback when unset or malformed: "example.merchant@upi", a deliberately
# fake placeholder. The UI labels the QR as a placeholder so nobody scans it
# expecting money to move. Set this to a real VPA to take a live payment.
# VITE_MERCHANT_VPA=yourshop@paytm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server (API functions only - not exposed to the browser)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional shared demo store. Without it every serverless instance keeps its
# own copy of the demo state, so a phone scanning the public dukaan QR may hit
# a different instance than the merchant device. /api/health reports which mode
# is live, and the public dukaan always falls back to the seeded sample shop.
#
# Read by: server/demoApi.ts
# Accepts either the Vercel KV names or the raw Upstash names; KV wins.
# Both the URL and the token must be set, otherwise shared mode stays off.
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=your-rest-token
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-rest-token
